# Testing Conventions

## Framework

- **Vitest** across all packages — not Jest
- `globals: true` in vitest config — no need to import `describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi`

## Test File Naming & Location

```
stride-db/src/tests/repositories/task.repo.test.ts
stride-core/src/tests/services/task.service.test.ts
stride-desktop/src/tests/hooks/useSyncStatus.test.ts
```

## Repository Tests (stride-db)

Test against a real in-memory SQLite database, not mocks:

```typescript
import { taskRepo } from '../../repositories/task.repo';
import { createTestDb } from '../setup';
import type { Task } from '@stridetime/types';

describe('TaskRepository', () => {
  let db: any;

  beforeEach(() => {
    db = createTestDb(); // In-memory SQLite via better-sqlite3
  });

  describe('create', () => {
    it('creates a task and returns it with a generated id', async () => {
      const input: Omit<Task, 'id'> = {
        title: 'Test Task',
        status: TaskStatus.TODO,
        // ... other required fields
      };
      const result = await taskRepo.create(db, input);
      expect(result.id).toBeTruthy();
      expect(result.title).toBe('Test Task');
    });
  });

  describe('findById', () => {
    it('returns null for a non-existent id', async () => {
      const result = await taskRepo.findById(db, 'does-not-exist');
      expect(result).toBeNull();
    });

    it('does not return soft-deleted records', async () => {
      const task = await taskRepo.create(db, validTaskInput);
      await taskRepo.delete(db, task.id);
      const result = await taskRepo.findById(db, task.id);
      expect(result).toBeNull();
    });
  });
});
```

**Minimum 6 tests per new repository:** CRUD operations + soft delete behavior + edge cases.

## Service Tests (stride-core)

Mock the repository — test service logic in isolation:

```typescript
// Hoist mocks BEFORE imports
const { mockTaskRepo } = vi.hoisted(() => ({
  mockTaskRepo: {
    create: vi.fn(),
    findById: vi.fn(),
    update: vi.fn(),
    delete: vi.fn(),
  },
}));

vi.mock('@stridetime/db', () => ({
  taskRepo: mockTaskRepo,
  TaskRepository: vi.fn(),
}));

describe('TaskService', () => {
  let service: TaskService;
  let mockDb: any;

  beforeEach(() => {
    service = new TaskService(mockTaskRepo);
    mockDb = {};
    vi.clearAllMocks();
  });

  it('throws ValidationError when title is empty', async () => {
    await expect(
      service.create(mockDb, { title: '', projectId: 'p1' })
    ).rejects.toThrow(ValidationError);
    expect(mockTaskRepo.create).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });

  it('throws NotFoundError when project does not exist', async () => {
    mockTaskRepo.findById.mockResolvedValue(null);
    await expect(
      service.create(mockDb, { title: 'Task', projectId: 'missing' })
    ).rejects.toThrow(NotFoundError);
  });

  it('creates a task with valid params', async () => {
    mockTaskRepo.findById.mockResolvedValue(validProject);
    mockTaskRepo.create.mockResolvedValue({ id: '1', title: 'Task' });
    const result = await service.create(mockDb, validInput);
    expect(mockTaskRepo.create).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
      mockDb,
      expect.objectContaining({ title: 'Task' })
    );
    expect(result.id).toBe('1');
  });
});
```

**Minimum 8 tests per new service:** validation errors + not-found paths + happy path + sanitization.

## Test Quality Rules

- Test observable behavior — not internal implementation details
- One assertion focus per test (a test can have multiple `expect` calls if they verify one behavior)
- Test names read as: `it('does X when Y')`
- `vi.clearAllMocks()` in `beforeEach` — never share mock state between tests
- Never commit code that breaks existing tests
- Run `yarn build && yarn test` in all affected packages before committing
